# Accepted image vulnerabilities (Trivy), one id per line with the reason and an expiry (exp:), after which the scan
# reports them again. Only add ones that have no fix or do not apply, after reading them.
#
# Reviewed 2026-11-06 (Phase 5.4). autocare-api: pcre2 10.32-3.el8_6 is not Debian's (that one is patched,
# 10.42-1+deb12u2) but the copy bundled inside the psycopg-binary wheel (psycopg_binary.libs/libpcre2-8-*.so, built on
# a RHEL 8 manylinux image; unchanged in the latest wheel, 3.3.8). Red Hat backports fixes into el8 builds, so the
# Debian fixed versions Trivy compares with do not apply; it is loaded only by the bundled libselinux and never
# compiles untrusted regular expressions. Removing it means dropping psycopg-binary for a source build against
# Debian's libpq (follow-up), not a safe change in a hardening phase.
